Section: utils
Priority: optional
Description: Push-to-talk local Whisper transcription for Linux
 omnihear lets you hold a hotkey to record audio and have it
 transcribed locally via faster-whisper (no cloud, no network calls
 during use), then typed directly into whichever field has focus.
 .
 Works on X11 and Wayland (GNOME, KDE, wlroots). On Wayland, add your
 user to the `input` group for hotkeys (`sudo usermod -aG input $USER`,
 then re-login); typing uses a built-in /dev/uinput virtual keyboard
 enabled by the bundled udev rule. Run `omnihear --doctor` to check
 your setup.

